IMPORT daydate

-- Criminal Injuries Compensation Act 2003 (WA) -- the date arithmetic the baseline needs, kept in one small module so
-- that the daydate library is imported once. Every other module of this encoding imports this one, not daydate.
--
-- Periods "within N years after", "within N days after" and "before ... reaches N years of age" are reckoned the plain
-- way: the period starts the day after the event and ends at the end of the same date N years on (29 February clamps to
-- 28 February), or the Nth day after the event. The Interpretation Act 1984 rules on reckoning time (for example a last
-- day on which an office is closed) are borrowed and not encoded beyond this.

§ `Criminal Injuries Compensation Act 2003 -- dates`

-- A date written day, month, year (for the other modules and the cases file, which do not import daydate).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or before` b IF Day a AT MOST Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls before` b IF Day a LESS THAN Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls after` b IF Day a GREATER THAN Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or after` b IF Day a AT LEAST Day b

-- The number of days from a to b (for the regulative rules, whose WITHIN counts days).
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` a `to` b MEANS Day b MINUS Day a

-- The same date n years on (29 February clamps to 28 February).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `years after` d MEANS `add years` d n

-- The nth day after d.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The later of two dates.
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF Day a AT LEAST Day b
        THEN a
        ELSE b
